Gruff Plum the elven Rangerette watched a chameleon charge right at her; 
and turn into a kitten after the first round. For the record, chameleons 
make excellent pets. This one (had) a tendency to change into a purple 
worm. The first time I heard a burp, the Oracle was pet food. So, leash 
up the Chameleon, keep in the proximity of those friendly green and grey 
elves, and soon enough Chameleon is burping up a full kit of elven 
weapons and armor. Nice kitty!

For a while, the tactical requisite was to maneuver Chameleon into play 
when its form was rather indestructilbe; and move Chameleon away from 
monsters when in the form of something less hardy. Piranahas and rock 
moles don't move very well when you pull on the leash.

PS I almost YASD when I stupidly broke a wand of light; Chameleon was 
not so lucky.

